hydrasdr-host (1.1.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Int16 DDC: saturate near ADC full scale instead of wrapping to the
    opposite sign (Float32 is not affected).
  * Conversion tables cover every 16-bit word (no more undefined shifts).
  * Windows: WinUSB RAW_IO with libusb 1.0.30 or later, for more USB
    throughput on a slow PC (an older libusb works as before).
  * Fix a crash on macOS when the device is unplugged while streaming.
  * Fix a crash when the sample rate changes while streaming; rate and
    bandwidth changes no longer reset the USB endpoint.
  * Stop and close wait for every USB transfer, a start, packing or sample
    type change while streaming returns HYDRASDR_ERROR_BUSY.
  * Open no longer resets a device that is already configured (spiflash
    requests time out instead of blocking).
  * hydrasdr_rx: unpacked RAW captures write the number of samples asked.

 -- Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@hydrasdr.com>  Tue, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

hydrasdr-host (1.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Windows ARM64 and ARM64EC support (MSVC builds).
    The ARM64EC hydrasdr.dll is a drop-in for x64 applications running under
    emulation on Windows 11 on ARM, keeping their x64 libusb-1.0.dll.
  * MSVC builds download libusb 1.0.30.
  * Linux zip archives: the tools now find the bundled libhydrasdr.so next
    to them instead of requiring an installed copy.
  * Packages: add Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (x86_64 and ARM64), Linux Mint 22.2 and
    22.3, AlmaLinux 10, Fedora 43 and 44.
    Drop the end-of-life Debian 11, Ubuntu 20.04, Fedora 41 and 42, and the
    Ubuntu 22.04 ARM64 package.

 -- Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@hydrasdr.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

hydrasdr-host (1.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libhydrasdr decimation stages (2x to 64x): fix the halfband ring
    buffers, 32 and 16 entries for 33 and 17 taps, whose batched stores
    overwrote the oldest history samples before the FIR read them. Every
    signal in a decimated band had images half (and, for int16 at 2x to
    8x, a quarter of) the output sample rate away, 43 to 57 dB below it.
    The stages now match a direct convolution bit-exactly.
  * Int16 stages: round the output shift instead of truncating it, which
    removes a DC line of 0.5 LSB per stage (-71 dBc at 64x for a -6 dBFS
    tone).
  * Int16 stages: unity gain per stage (output shift 15 on the Q15 taps)
    instead of 2x per stage. The int16 level at any decimation now
    matches 1x and float32; clients that compensated the old +6 dB per
    stage must drop that correction. Strong signals no longer clip at
    high decimation (the old chain clipped above -36 dBFS at 64x).

 -- Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@hydrasdr.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

hydrasdr-host (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename binary package libhydrasdr0 to libhydrasdr1 to match the
    shared library SONAME (libhydrasdr.so.1, SOVERSION=1 since v1.0.4).
    Fixes lintian package-name-doesnt-match-sonames warning.
  * Update libhydrasdr-dev and hydrasdr-host Depends accordingly.
  * Rename debian/libhydrasdr0.{install,dirs,udev} to libhydrasdr1.*
    and update debian/rules.

